# L0 semantic challenge round 1.
1 UPHELD | SEC-007's text; nothing added.
2 UPHELD | 'When it makes code clearer, safer or simpler' does not exceed RUN-009's 'when it improves clarity' enough to change behavior: no mechanical duty, and the same clause forbids nothing RUN-009 allows.
3 UPHELD | 'Before writing code' is GOV-018's 'before implementing' and GOV-017's prior approval.
4 UPHELD | 'Consider' lists an option under RUN-016; a reused key with a different payload is a request conflicting with state under API-006. Weaker strength stays recorded.
5 UPHELD | Keeps tests from Development and Production data (TST-004); knowledge-skill imperative at DEFAULT per A1.
6 UPHELD | 'Not mandatory' agrees with DEP-020 and DEP-011; 'review carefully' is a weaker form of RUN-016.
7 UPHELD | A routing table has no behavior beyond the owning workflows; no policy names these routes.
8 UPHELD | Artifact placement concerns the instruction system only.
9 UPHELD | A checker run after instruction edits; product code is unaffected.
10 UPHELD | Report content beyond verification states; a truthful report without it satisfies WF-009.
11 UPHELD | Probe mechanics are EXC-006/EXC-010 technique; no API policy reaches them.
12 REVISED_NEEDED | The scenario does not distinguish. A test using WebApplicationFactory<Program> needs Program accessible, and 'for example' leaves the form open, so any behavior meeting TST-006 this way also meets the claim. The calibration reading (NN) was right and B016 departed from it. Corrected by COR-L0-0001.
13 UPHELD | A flagged finding asking for a recorded decision or reported reason is more than DEP-020's exception status, and it is advisory, so the strength is not comparable.
14 UPHELD | A free-form approval satisfies GOV-017, and the five-field format and recording do not follow from it.
15 UPHELD | Blocks a flag used for any purpose, while DEP-025 limits only its use to bypass peers.
16 UPHELD | Instruction-layer status and an approval route have different actions.
17 UPHELD | A definition and a preference can be read apart.
18 UPHELD | Removal is an added duty; 'no unrelated cleanup' is GOV-014's. Their outcomes differ.
